module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.BitUniformityIII.DivisibleMaps
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The duality step of Tag 0GAC: the section `σ'` of `p^*(M^∨)`

The proof of [Stacks, Tag 0GAC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GAC) turns an `A`-linear
map `φ : M → Iⁿ/I^{2n}` into a section `σ'` of a twist of `p^*(M^∨)` whose evaluation against
the elements of `M` is `φ` twisted down to that level. It does so in three moves: the map
`χ : p^*M → 𝒪_{Yₙ}(n)` that `φ` induces determines a section `σ ∈ Γ(X, (p^*M)^∨(n))`, because
`𝒪_{Yₙ}(n)` is invertible; the kernel and cokernel of `can : p^*(M^∨) → (p^*M)^∨` are scheme
theoretically supported on `Y_c` (Remark 0GAB), so by Tag 0GA9 the canonical map
`(p^*M)^∨(n) → (p^*M)^∨(n - 2c)` factors through `p^*(M^∨)(n - 2c)`; and the image of `σ`
under that factorization is `σ'`.

`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.DualSituation` carries the evaluation dictionary of
Remark 0GAB but nothing about `(p^*M)^∨`, so this step cannot be taken there;
`DualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul` and `DualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul_of_le` therefore
take `σ'` and its evaluation property as hypotheses on each pair `(M, φ)`. This file supplies the
missing data — `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.CanDualSituation`: the cohomology of the
twists of `(p^*M)^∨` and of the image, cokernel and kernel of `can`, the exact sequences relating
them, and the vanishing of the twisting maps on the cokernel and the kernel (Tag 0GA9, both
being supported on `Y_c` by Remark 0GAB) — and *derives* `σ'` and its evaluation property, so
that the resulting form of Tag 0GAC quantifies over every `M` and `φ` with no extra
hypothesis.

## The two halves of the factorization, and the case `d = 0`

The factorization through `can` is carried here as its two constituent steps rather than as one
`2c` drop, because they are governed by different inputs and the second is free when `d = 0`.
Writing `0 → ker(can) → p^*(M^∨) → im(can) → 0` and `0 → im(can) → (p^*M)^∨ → coker(can) → 0`:

* the **cokernel** step spends one `c`. The image of `σ` in `Γ(coker(can)(n))` dies in
  `Γ(coker(can)(n - c))` because `coker(can)` is supported on `Y_c` and Tag 0GA9 makes
  `coker(can)(q) → coker(can)(q - c)` zero, so by left exactness of `Γ` the image of `σ` in
  `Γ((p^*M)^∨(n - c))` comes from `Γ(im(can)(n - c))`. This is `exists_imgToDual_eq_Hdualtr`.
* the **kernel** step spends one more `c` in general: the image of a section of `im(can)(q)` in
  `Γ(im(can)(q - c))` lifts to `H⁰(X, p^*(M^∨)(q - c))` because its obstruction in
  `H¹(X, ker(can)(q - c))` is the image of one in `H¹(X, ker(can)(q))` under a map that is zero,
  again by Tag 0GA9 and the `Y_c`-support of `ker(can)`. This is `exists_canToImg_eq_Himgtr`.
* when `d = 0` the kernel step costs **nothing**: `d` bounds the fibre dimensions of
  `p : X → Spec(A)`, so `H¹(X, ℱ) = 0` for every coherent `ℱ`, in particular for
  `ker(can)(q)`, and by the long exact sequence of `0 → ker(can) → p^*(M^∨) → im(can) → 0`
  the map `H⁰(X, p^*(M^∨)(q)) → Γ(X, im(can)(q))` is already surjective. This is the theorem
  `surjective_canToImg`, proved from the exactness `exact_canToImg` of that sequence and the
  vanishing `vanishing_Hker` above `d`.

That is what makes the `d = 0` case of the tag come out at the levels the tag states. The
source writes "The case `d = 0`. Argument is exactly the same as in the case `d = 1`", which
produces `σ'` at level `n - 2c`, one `c` short of what its own `d = 0` conclusion — the
identity at `I^{n-c}/I^{2n-c}` with `ψᵢ` into `I^{n-2c}/I^{2n-2c}` — needs. Spending the
cokernel `c` only, which `d = 0` permits, lands exactly there.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.CanDualSituation`: a `DualSituation` together with the
  cohomology of the twists of `(p^*M)^∨` and of the image, cokernel and kernel of `can`, the
  section `σ` attached to a homomorphism `φ`, the exact sequences relating them, and the
  vanishing of the twisting maps on the cokernel and the kernel.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.CanDualSituation.dualSectionOfHom`: the section `σ'`,
  at the level `n - 2c` reached by spending both `c`'s.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.principalCanDualSituation`: the witness in which `I` is
  generated by a single nonzerodivisor, so that `p` is an isomorphism *and* every `𝒪_X(q)` is
  invertible — the case the docstring of `affineSituation` names.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.DualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul_of_le`: everything
  in Tag 0GAC after the duality step, from a section `σ'` at an arbitrary level `e ≤ n`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.CanDualSituation.surjective_canToImg`: for `d = 0` the
  map `H⁰(X, p^*(M^∨)(q)) → Γ(X, im(can)(q))` is surjective.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.CanDualSituation.ev_dualSectionOfHom` and
  `exists_ev_eq_of_d_eq_zero`: the evaluation property of `σ'`, at level `n - 2c` in general
  and at level `n - c` when `d = 0`. This is the hypothesis `hσ` of
  `DualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul_of_le`, discharged.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.CanDualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul`: **Tag 0GAC**,
  at the source's own levels for every `d` and with no hypothesis the source does not make.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.bijective_dualHomTensorLift_span_singleton`: for
  `I = (x)` with `x` a nonzerodivisor the canonical map
  `(I^q/I^{q+n}) ⊗_A M^∨ → Hom_A(M, I^q/I^{q+n})` is bijective, which is what makes the witness
  non-degenerate rather than a tower of zero modules.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GAC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GAC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GAB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GAB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA9)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace DualSituation

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A} {n c : ℕ}
  (S : DualSituation A I n c)

/-- Everything in Stacks Tag 0GAC after the duality step, from a section `σ'` of
`p^*(M^∨)` at an arbitrary level `e ≤ n` whose evaluation is `φ` truncated to level `e`.

With `k + 1 = max(d, 1)`, `g + c = f` and `f + kc = e`, the composition
`M --φ--> Iⁿ/I^{2n} → I^f/I^{f+n}` is of the form `∑ aᵢψᵢ` with `aᵢ ∈ I^c` and
`ψᵢ : M → I^g/I^{g+n}`. The `kc` drop from `e` to `f` is Tag 0GAA clause (5) for `d ≥ 2` and
clause (4) for `d ≤ 1` (`exists_ev_secM_eq`), and the passage from the resulting element of
`I^f ⊗_A M^∨` to the sum is `ev_secM_mem_divisibleMaps`.

The level of `σ'` is left free because it depends on `d`: the duality step reaches `n - 2c`
in general but only spends one `c` when `d = 0`. `DualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul` is the
case `e + 2c = n`; `CanDualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul` supplies `σ'` and is where
Tag 0GAC is stated with no hypothesis on `σ'`. -/
theorem exists_sum_powQuotSmul_of_le (M : ANCModule I n c)
    (φ : resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I n n) {g f e k : ℕ}
    (hgf : g + c = f) (hk : max S.d 1 = k + 1) (he : f + k * c = e) (hen : e ≤ n)
    (hq : S.q₀ ≤ f) (σ' : S.H M.dual 0 (e : ℤ))
    (hσ : S.ev M e (hq.trans (Nat.le.intro he)) σ' = (powQuotLe I hen).comp φ) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (a : Fin N → A) (ha : ∀ i, a i ∈ I ^ c)
      (ψ : Fin N → (resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I g n)),
      (powQuotLe I ((Nat.le.intro he).trans hen)).comp φ =
        ∑ i, (powQuotSmul I (ha i) hgf).comp (ψ i) := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := S.exists_ev_secM_eq M hk he hq σ'
  have key : (powQuotLe I ((Nat.le.intro he).trans hen)).comp φ =
      S.ev M f hq (S.secM M.dual f t) := by
    rw [ht, hσ]
    exact LinearMap.ext fun z =>
      (powQuotLe_powQuotLe I n hen (Nat.le.intro he) (φ z)).symm
  rw [key]
  exact exists_sum_of_mem_divisibleMaps I n c hgf (S.ev_secM_mem_divisibleMaps M hgf hq t)

end DualSituation

/-- The data and the standing hypotheses of the *duality step* of Stacks Tag 0GAC: a
`DualSituation` together with the sections of the twists of the dual `(p^*M)^∨` of the pullback,
of the image and of the cokernel of `can : p^*(M^∨) → (p^*M)^∨`, the first cohomology of the
twists of its kernel, the maps between them, the section of `(p^*M)^∨(q)` attached to a
homomorphism `M → I^q/I^{q+n}`, and the properties of these that the Stacks Project establishes
before Tag 0GAC.

Each input is carried as data for the same reason as the cohomology modules of `Situation`,
`ModuleSituation` and `TwistedModuleSituation` and as `DualSituation.ev`: the scheme `X` and its
sheaves do not appear in this development, so a fact about them can only enter as part of the
Situation. Writing `0 → ker(can) → p^*(M^∨) → im(can) → 0` and
`0 → im(can) → (p^*M)^∨ → coker(can) → 0`:

* `secDual` is "since `𝒪_{Yₙ}(n)` is invertible on `Yₙ` the linear map `χ` determines a section
  `σ ∈ Γ(X, (p^*M)^∨(n))`", together with Tag 0GA7(2), which is what produces `χ` from `φ`;
  `evDual` is evaluation against the elements of `M`, and `evDual_secDual` says it recovers `φ`.
* `canToImg` and `imgToDual` are `can` factored through its image, and `evDual_can` is the
  commuting square `p^*e_z` / `e_{p^*z}` of the proof of Tag 0GAC, which says that evaluating
  `can(t)` against `z ∈ M` is evaluating `t` against `z` — i.e. that `evDual` extends `ev`.
* `exact_imgToDual` is the left exactness of `Γ` on the second sequence, and `exact_canToImg`
  the long exact sequence of the first at `Γ(X, im(can)(q))`, with connecting map `canToImgδ`;
  `dualToCoker_Hdualtr` and `canToImgδ_Himgtr` are their naturality in the twist. They are the
  analogues of `ModuleSituation.exact_pullback` and `TwistedModuleSituation.pullbackToImage_tr`.
* `Hcokertr_eq_zero` and `Hkertr_eq_zero` are Tag 0GA9 for `coker(can)` and `ker(can)`: by
  Remark 0GAB (`IsANCModule.cokernel_map_pullbackModuleDualMap_eq_zero` and its kernel
  companion) both are annihilated by `I^c`, i.e. scheme theoretically supported on `Y_c`, so
  the canonical maps `coker(can)(q) → coker(can)(q - c)` and `ker(can)(q) → ker(can)(q - c)`
  are zero, hence so are the maps they induce on cohomology.
* `vanishing_Hker` is the vanishing of `Hⁱ(X, ℱ)` for coherent `ℱ` and `i > d`, at
  `ℱ = ker(can)(q)` and `i = 1`; it is the analogue of `ModuleSituation.vanishing_HF`.

What is *not* assumed is the duality step itself, nor any factorization through `can`. That the
canonical map `(p^*M)^∨(n) → (p^*M)^∨(n - 2c)` factors through `p^*(M^∨)(n - 2c)` on sections —
the step the source calls Tag 0GA9 with "small detail omitted" — is proved from the two exact
sequences and the two vanishing twisting maps (`exists_imgToDual_eq_Hdualtr` and
`exists_canToImg_eq_Himgtr`), and that when `d = 0` the kernel step is free is proved from
`vanishing_Hker` (`surjective_canToImg`). From these, `dualSectionOfHom` builds `σ'` from `φ`
and `ev_dualSectionOfHom` proves its evaluation property. Nothing in the structure mentions a
particular `M` or `φ`.

The levels are natural numbers rather than integers, since every twist the duality step visits
lies between `n - 2c` and `n`; a lower level is carried as a parameter `e` with `e + c = q`, as
everywhere else in this section, so that no truncated subtraction appears in a type.

See `principalCanDualSituation` for a witness in which `secDual` is bijective. -/
structure CanDualSituation (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    (n c : ℕ) extends DualSituation A I n c where
  /-- `Hdual M q` is `Γ(X, (p^*M)^∨(q))`, the sections of the twists of the dual of `p^*M`. -/
  Hdual : ANCModule I n c → ℕ → ModuleCat.{u} A
  /-- The canonical map `(p^*M)^∨(q) → (p^*M)^∨(q')` on sections, for `q' ≤ q`. -/
  Hdualtr : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q q' : ℕ), q' ≤ q → Hdual M q →ₗ[A] Hdual M q'
  /-- `Himg M q` is `Γ(X, im(can)(q))`, the sections of the twists of the image of `can`. -/
  Himg : ANCModule I n c → ℕ → ModuleCat.{u} A
  /-- The canonical map `im(can)(q) → im(can)(q')` on sections, for `q' ≤ q`. -/
  Himgtr : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q q' : ℕ), q' ≤ q → Himg M q →ₗ[A] Himg M q'
  /-- `Hcoker M q` is `Γ(X, coker(can)(q))`, the sections of the twists of the cokernel of
  `can`. -/
  Hcoker : ANCModule I n c → ℕ → ModuleCat.{u} A
  /-- The canonical map `coker(can)(q) → coker(can)(q')` on sections, for `q' ≤ q`. -/
  Hcokertr : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q q' : ℕ), q' ≤ q → Hcoker M q →ₗ[A] Hcoker M q'
  /-- `Hker M q` is `H¹(X, ker(can)(q))`, for the kernel of `can`. -/
  Hker : ANCModule I n c → ℕ → ModuleCat.{u} A
  /-- The map `H¹(X, ker(can)(q)) → H¹(X, ker(can)(q'))` induced by the canonical map, for
  `q' ≤ q`. -/
  Hkertr : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q q' : ℕ), q' ≤ q → Hker M q →ₗ[A] Hker M q'
  /-- The section `σ ∈ Γ(X, (p^*M)^∨(q))` determined by a homomorphism
  `φ : M → I^q/I^{q+n}`: the map `χ : p^*M → 𝒪_{Yₙ}(q)` that `φ` induces through Tag 0GA7(2),
  read as a section of `(p^*M)^∨(q)` using that `𝒪_{Yₙ}(q)` is invertible. -/
  secDual : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ),
    (resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I q n) →ₗ[A] Hdual M q
  /-- Evaluating a section of `(p^*M)^∨(q)` against the elements of `M`, defined for
  `q ≥ q(S)`, where Tag 0GA7(2) identifies `Γ(Yₙ, 𝒪_{Yₙ}(q))` with `I^q/I^{q+n}`. -/
  evDual : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ), toSituation.q₀ ≤ q →
    Hdual M q →ₗ[A] (resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I q n)
  /-- Evaluating the section attached to `φ` returns `φ`. -/
  evDual_secDual : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ) (hq : toSituation.q₀ ≤ q)
      (φ : resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I q n), evDual M q hq (secDual M q φ) = φ
  /-- The evaluation is natural in the twist. -/
  evDual_Hdualtr : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q q' : ℕ) (hq : toSituation.q₀ ≤ q)
      (hq' : toSituation.q₀ ≤ q') (h : q' ≤ q) (σ : Hdual M q),
    evDual M q' hq' (Hdualtr M q q' h σ) = (powQuotLe I h).comp (evDual M q hq σ)
  /-- The map `H⁰(X, p^*(M^∨)(q)) → Γ(X, im(can)(q))` of the `can` of Remark 0GAB onto its
  image. -/
  canToImg : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ),
    toModuleSituation.H M.dual 0 (q : ℤ) →ₗ[A] Himg M q
  /-- The inclusion `Γ(X, im(can)(q)) → Γ(X, (p^*M)^∨(q))`. -/
  imgToDual : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ), Himg M q →ₗ[A] Hdual M q
  /-- The map `Γ(X, (p^*M)^∨(q)) → Γ(X, coker(can)(q))`. -/
  dualToCoker : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ), Hdual M q →ₗ[A] Hcoker M q
  /-- The connecting map `Γ(X, im(can)(q)) → H¹(X, ker(can)(q))` of
  `0 → ker(can) → p^*(M^∨) → im(can) → 0`. -/
  canToImgδ : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ), Himg M q →ₗ[A] Hker M q
  /-- The inclusion of the image is natural in the twist. -/
  imgToDual_Himgtr : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q q' : ℕ) (h : q' ≤ q) (t : Himg M q),
    imgToDual M q' (Himgtr M q q' h t) = Hdualtr M q q' h (imgToDual M q t)
  /-- The map to the cokernel is natural in the twist. -/
  dualToCoker_Hdualtr : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q q' : ℕ) (h : q' ≤ q) (σ : Hdual M q),
    dualToCoker M q' (Hdualtr M q q' h σ) = Hcokertr M q q' h (dualToCoker M q σ)
  /-- The connecting map is natural in the twist. -/
  canToImgδ_Himgtr : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q q' : ℕ) (h : q' ≤ q) (t : Himg M q),
    canToImgδ M q' (Himgtr M q q' h t) = Hkertr M q q' h (canToImgδ M q t)
  /-- Left exactness of `Γ(X, -)` on `0 → im(can) → (p^*M)^∨ → coker(can) → 0`, at
  `Γ(X, (p^*M)^∨(q))`. -/
  exact_imgToDual : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ),
    Function.Exact (imgToDual M q) (dualToCoker M q)
  /-- Exactness of the long exact sequence of `0 → ker(can) → p^*(M^∨) → im(can) → 0` at
  `Γ(X, im(can)(q))`. -/
  exact_canToImg : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ),
    Function.Exact (canToImg M q) (canToImgδ M q)
  /-- Evaluating `can(t)` against `z ∈ M` is evaluating `t` against `z`: the commuting square
  of `p^*e_z` and `e_{p^*z}` in the proof of Tag 0GAC, which holds by functoriality of the
  construction `can`. -/
  evDual_can : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ) (hq : toSituation.q₀ ≤ q)
      (t : toModuleSituation.H M.dual 0 (q : ℤ)),
    evDual M q hq (imgToDual M q (canToImg M q t)) = toDualSituation.ev M q hq t
  /-- Tag 0GA9 for the cokernel of `can`, which is supported on `Y_c` by Remark 0GAB: the
  canonical map `coker(can)(q) → coker(can)(q - c)` is zero, hence so is the map it induces on
  sections. The lower twist is a parameter `e` with `e + c = q`. -/
  Hcokertr_eq_zero : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q e : ℕ) (h : e ≤ q), e + c = q →
    Hcokertr M q e h = 0
  /-- Tag 0GA9 for the kernel of `can`, which is supported on `Y_c` by Remark 0GAB: the
  canonical map `ker(can)(q) → ker(can)(q - c)` is zero, hence so is the map it induces on
  `H¹`. -/
  Hkertr_eq_zero : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q e : ℕ) (h : e ≤ q), e + c = q →
    Hkertr M q e h = 0
  /-- `Hⁱ(X, ℱ) = 0` for coherent `ℱ` and `i > d`, since `d` bounds the fibre dimensions of `p`,
  applied to `ℱ = ker(can)(q)` and `i = 1`. -/
  vanishing_Hker : ∀ (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ), toSituation.d < 1 → Subsingleton (Hker M q)

namespace CanDualSituation

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A} {n c : ℕ}
  (S : CanDualSituation A I n c)

/-- **The cokernel half of the factorization through `can`.** The image of a section of
`(p^*M)^∨(q)` in `Γ(X, (p^*M)^∨(q - c))` is a section of `im(can)(q - c)`: its image in
`Γ(X, coker(can)(q - c))` is the image of a section of `coker(can)(q)` under the canonical map,
which is zero because `coker(can)` is supported on `Y_c`, so it lies in the image of
`Γ(X, im(can)(q - c))` by left exactness of `Γ`. -/
theorem exists_imgToDual_eq_Hdualtr (M : ANCModule I n c) {q e : ℕ} (heq : e + c = q)
    (σ : S.Hdual M q) :
    ∃ t : S.Himg M e, S.imgToDual M e t = S.Hdualtr M q e (Nat.le.intro heq) σ := by
  refine (S.exact_imgToDual M e _).1 ?_
  rw [S.dualToCoker_Hdualtr, S.Hcokertr_eq_zero M q e _ heq, LinearMap.zero_apply]

/-- **The kernel half of the factorization through `can`.** The image of a section of
`im(can)(q)` in `Γ(X, im(can)(q - c))` lifts to `H⁰(X, p^*(M^∨)(q - c))`: its obstruction in
`H¹(X, ker(can)(q - c))` is the image of an element of `H¹(X, ker(can)(q))` under the map the
canonical map induces, which is zero because `ker(can)` is supported on `Y_c`. -/
theorem exists_canToImg_eq_Himgtr (M : ANCModule I n c) {q e : ℕ} (heq : e + c = q)
    (t : S.Himg M q) :
    ∃ s : S.H M.dual 0 (e : ℤ), S.canToImg M e s = S.Himgtr M q e (Nat.le.intro heq) t := by
  refine (S.exact_canToImg M e _).1 ?_
  rw [S.canToImgδ_Himgtr, S.Hkertr_eq_zero M q e _ heq, LinearMap.zero_apply]

/-- For `d = 0` the map `H⁰(X, p^*(M^∨)(q)) → Γ(X, im(can)(q))` onto the image of `can` is
surjective: the next term `H¹(X, ker(can)(q))` of the long exact sequence of
`0 → ker(can) → p^*(M^∨) → im(can) → 0` vanishes, because `d` bounds the fibre dimensions of
`p`. This is what makes the kernel step of the duality step free when `d = 0`. -/
theorem surjective_canToImg (hd : S.d = 0) (M : ANCModule I n c) (q : ℕ) :
    Function.Surjective (S.canToImg M q) := by
  have : Subsingleton (S.Hker M q) := S.vanishing_Hker M q (by omega)
  exact fun t => (S.exact_canToImg M q t).1 (Subsingleton.elim _ _)

/-- The cokernel half of the duality step of Stacks Tag 0GAC: the section `σ` of `(p^*M)^∨(n)`
that `φ` determines, pushed one twist down into the sections of `im(can)(n - c)`, which is
possible because `coker(can)` is supported on `Y_c` (`exists_imgToDual_eq_Hdualtr`). -/
noncomputable def imgSectionOfHom (M : ANCModule I n c)
    (φ : resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I n n) (e : ℕ) (hen : e + c = n) : S.Himg M e :=
  (S.exists_imgToDual_eq_Hdualtr M hen (S.secDual M n φ)).choose

/-- `imgSectionOfHom` is a preimage, under the inclusion of the image of `can`, of the section
`σ` that `φ` determines, twisted down to level `n - c`. -/
theorem imgToDual_imgSectionOfHom (M : ANCModule I n c)
    (φ : resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I n n) (e : ℕ) (hen : e + c = n) :
    S.imgToDual M e (S.imgSectionOfHom M φ e hen) =
      S.Hdualtr M n e (Nat.le.intro hen) (S.secDual M n φ) :=
  (S.exists_imgToDual_eq_Hdualtr M hen (S.secDual M n φ)).choose_spec

/-- Evaluating `imgSectionOfHom` against the elements of `M` is `φ` twisted down to level
`n - c`. -/
theorem evDual_imgToDual_imgSectionOfHom (M : ANCModule I n c)
    (φ : resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I n n) (e : ℕ) (hen : e + c = n) (hq : S.q₀ ≤ e) :
    S.evDual M e hq (S.imgToDual M e (S.imgSectionOfHom M φ e hen)) =
      (powQuotLe I (Nat.le.intro hen)).comp φ := by
  have hen' : e ≤ n := Nat.le.intro hen
  rw [S.imgToDual_imgSectionOfHom M φ e hen,
    S.evDual_Hdualtr M n e (hq.trans hen') hq hen', S.evDual_secDual M n (hq.trans hen') φ]

/-- **The duality step of Stacks Tag 0GAC.** The section `σ'` of `p^*(M^∨)(n - 2c)` the proof
of Tag 0GAC manufactures from an `A`-linear map `φ : M → Iⁿ/I^{2n}`: take the section `σ` of
`(p^*M)^∨(n)` that `φ` determines and spend one twist on the cokernel of `can`
(`exists_imgToDual_eq_Hdualtr`) and one on its kernel (`exists_canToImg_eq_Himgtr`), both
supported on `Y_c`.

The two levels are the parameters `e₁ = n - c` and `e = n - 2c`. -/
noncomputable def dualSectionOfHom (M : ANCModule I n c)
    (φ : resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I n n) (e e₁ : ℕ) (he : e + c = e₁)
    (hen : e₁ + c = n) : S.H M.dual 0 (e : ℤ) :=
  (S.exists_canToImg_eq_Himgtr M he (S.imgSectionOfHom M φ e₁ hen)).choose

/-- `dualSectionOfHom` is a preimage, under `can` onto its image, of `imgSectionOfHom` twisted
down to level `n - 2c`. -/
theorem canToImg_dualSectionOfHom (M : ANCModule I n c)
    (φ : resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I n n) (e e₁ : ℕ) (he : e + c = e₁)
    (hen : e₁ + c = n) :
    S.canToImg M e (S.dualSectionOfHom M φ e e₁ he hen) =
      S.Himgtr M e₁ e (Nat.le.intro he) (S.imgSectionOfHom M φ e₁ hen) :=
  (S.exists_canToImg_eq_Himgtr M he (S.imgSectionOfHom M φ e₁ hen)).choose_spec

/-- The evaluation property of `σ'`: evaluating `dualSectionOfHom` against the elements of `M`
is `φ` twisted down to level `n - 2c`. This is the hypothesis `hσ` of
`DualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul_of_le`, discharged.

The source's argument: evaluating `σ'` is evaluating `can(σ')` (`evDual_can`), which is the
image of the cokernel step (`canToImg_dualSectionOfHom` and `imgToDual_Himgtr`), whose
evaluation is `φ` twisted down (`evDual_imgToDual_imgSectionOfHom`). -/
theorem ev_dualSectionOfHom (M : ANCModule I n c)
    (φ : resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I n n) (e e₁ : ℕ) (he : e + c = e₁)
    (hen : e₁ + c = n) (hq : S.q₀ ≤ e) (hn : e ≤ n) :
    S.ev M e hq (S.dualSectionOfHom M φ e e₁ he hen) = (powQuotLe I hn).comp φ := by
  have h1 : e ≤ e₁ := Nat.le.intro he
  have h2 : e₁ ≤ n := Nat.le.intro hen
  rw [← S.evDual_can M e hq, S.canToImg_dualSectionOfHom M φ e e₁ he hen,
    S.imgToDual_Himgtr M e₁ e h1, S.evDual_Hdualtr M e₁ e (hq.trans h1) hq h1,
    S.evDual_imgToDual_imgSectionOfHom M φ e₁ hen (hq.trans h1)]
  exact LinearMap.ext fun z => powQuotLe_powQuotLe I n h2 h1 (φ z)

/-- The duality step when `d = 0`, where it spends only the cokernel's twist: `σ'` is obtained
at level `n - c` rather than `n - 2c`, because `H⁰(X, p^*(M^∨)(q)) → Γ(X, im(can)(q))` is
surjective once `H¹(X, ker(can)(q))` vanishes (`surjective_canToImg`).

This is what brings the `d = 0` case of Tag 0GAC out at the levels the tag states. -/
theorem exists_ev_eq_of_d_eq_zero (M : ANCModule I n c)
    (φ : resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I n n) (e : ℕ) (hd : S.d = 0) (hen : e + c = n)
    (hq : S.q₀ ≤ e) (hn : e ≤ n) :
    ∃ σ' : S.H M.dual 0 (e : ℤ), S.ev M e hq σ' = (powQuotLe I hn).comp φ := by
  obtain ⟨σ', hσ'⟩ := S.surjective_canToImg hd M e (S.imgSectionOfHom M φ e hen)
  refine ⟨σ', ?_⟩
  rw [← S.evDual_can M e hq, hσ']
  exact S.evDual_imgToDual_imgSectionOfHom M φ e hen hq

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0GAC.** With `q₀ = q(S)` and `d = d(S)`, let `M` be an
`(A, n, c)`-module and `φ : M → Iⁿ/I^{2n}` an `A`-linear map, and assume
`n ≥ max(q₀ + (1 + d)c, (2 + d)c)`. Then the composition

`M --φ--> Iⁿ/I^{2n} → I^{n-(1+d)c}/I^{2n-(1+d)c}`

is of the form `∑ aᵢψᵢ` with `aᵢ ∈ I^c` and `ψᵢ : M → I^{n-(2+d)c}/I^{2n-(2+d)c}`.

The levels are carried as parameters so that no truncated subtraction appears in a type:
`g + c = f` and `f + (1 + d)c = n`, so that `f = n - (1 + d)c` and `g = n - (2 + d)c`. The
source's two numerical hypotheses are exactly the existence of `g` as a natural number
(`n ≥ (2 + d)c`, since `n = g + (2 + d)c`) and `q₀ ≤ f` (`n ≥ q₀ + (1 + d)c`).

The source adds, for `d = 0` only, the hypothesis `n ≥ q₀ + 2c`. It is what its own `d = 0`
argument needs, that argument being "exactly the same as in the case `d = 1`" and so producing
`σ'` at level `n - 2c`; it is not needed here, because at `d = 0` the duality step spends only
the cokernel's twist and produces `σ'` at level `n - c` (`exists_ev_eq_of_d_eq_zero`). Omitting
a hypothesis the source grants strengthens the statement, so nothing of the tag is lost.

The proof splits on `d`. For `d ≥ 1` the duality step gives `σ'` at `e = n - 2c`
(`ev_dualSectionOfHom`) and Tag 0GAA clause (5) for `d ≥ 2`, clause (4) for `d = 1`, drops it
by `kc` with `k = d - 1` to level `f`. For `d = 0` the step gives `σ'` at `e = n - c = f`
directly and clause (4) drops nothing. Both finish through
`DualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul_of_le`.

`DualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul` in `DivisibleMaps.lean` also carries the tag, with a note
recording its two deviations: `max(d, 1)` in place of `d`, and `σ'` with its evaluation property
as hypotheses. This declaration has neither. It is stated over an abstract `CanDualSituation`;
the tag is registered on its instance at the blowup itself,
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityIII.exists_sum_powQuotSmul_blowup`, whose only hypotheses are the
tag's own. -/
theorem exists_sum_powQuotSmul (M : ANCModule I n c)
    (φ : resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I n n) {g f : ℕ}
    (hgf : g + c = f) (hf : f + (1 + S.d) * c = n) (hq : S.q₀ ≤ f) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (a : Fin N → A) (ha : ∀ i, a i ∈ I ^ c)
      (ψ : Fin N → (resModule I n M.1 →ₗ[A] powQuot I g n)),
      (powQuotLe I (Nat.le.intro hf)).comp φ =
        ∑ i, (powQuotSmul I (ha i) hgf).comp (ψ i) := by
  have hfn : f ≤ n := Nat.le.intro hf
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos S.d with hd | hd
  · have hen : f + c = n := by
      have h := hf
      rw [hd] at h
      omega
    obtain ⟨σ', hσ'⟩ := S.exists_ev_eq_of_d_eq_zero M φ f hd hen hq hfn
    exact DualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul_of_le S.toDualSituation M φ hgf
      (by rw [hd]; rfl) (by omega) hfn hq σ' hσ'
  · obtain ⟨k, hdk⟩ : ∃ k, S.d = k + 1 := ⟨S.d - 1, by omega⟩
    have hk : max S.d 1 = k + 1 := by rw [hdk]; exact max_eq_left (by omega)
    have hfe : f + k * c + c + c = n := by
      have h := hf
      rw [hdk, show (1 + (k + 1)) * c = k * c + c + c from by ring, ← add_assoc,
        ← add_assoc] at h
      exact h
    have hfe' : f + k * c ≤ n := by omega
    exact DualSituation.exists_sum_powQuotSmul_of_le S.toDualSituation M φ hgf hk rfl hfe' hq
      (S.dualSectionOfHom M φ (f + k * c) (f + k * c + c) rfl (by omega))
      (S.ev_dualSectionOfHom M φ (f + k * c) (f + k * c + c) rfl (by omega)
        (hq.trans (Nat.le_add_right f (k * c))) hfe')

end CanDualSituation

section PrincipalWitness

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (x : A) (n q : ℕ)

/-- For `I = (x)` the class of `x^q` in `I^q/I^{q+n}`. It generates that module over `A`
(`exists_smul_powQuotGen`), and freely so when `x` is a nonzerodivisor
(`smul_powQuotGen_eq_zero_iff`): this is the invertibility of `𝒪_X(q)` on the blowup of a
principal ideal, where the blowing up is an isomorphism. -/
noncomputable def powQuotGen : powQuot (Ideal.span {x}) q n :=
  Submodule.Quotient.mk ⟨x ^ q, by
    rw [Ideal.span_singleton_pow]
    exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _⟩

/-- For `I = (x)`, `a * x ^ q` lies in `I ^ q`. -/
private theorem mul_pow_mem_span_pow (a : A) :
    a * x ^ q ∈ ((Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ q : Ideal A) :=
  Ideal.mul_mem_left _ a (Ideal.pow_mem_pow (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self x) q)

/-- For `I = (x)`, the multiple `a • powQuotGen x n q` is the class of `a * x ^ q` in
`I^q/I^{q+n}`. -/
theorem smul_powQuotGen (a : A)
    (h : a * x ^ q ∈ ((Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ q : Ideal A)) :
    a • powQuotGen x n q =
      (Submodule.Quotient.mk ⟨a * x ^ q, h⟩ : powQuot (Ideal.span {x}) q n) := rfl

/-- The class of `x^q` generates `I^q/I^{q+n}` over `A`, for `I = (x)`. -/
theorem exists_smul_powQuotGen (y : powQuot (Ideal.span {x}) q n) :
    ∃ a : A, y = a • powQuotGen x n q := by
  induction y using Submodule.Quotient.induction_on with
  | H z =>
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := z
    rw [Ideal.span_singleton_pow, Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at hz
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hz
    refine ⟨a, ?_⟩
    rw [smul_powQuotGen x n q a (mul_pow_mem_span_pow x q a)]
    exact congrArg Submodule.Quotient.mk (Subtype.ext (mul_comm _ _))

/-- For `I = (x)` with `x` a nonzerodivisor, `a·x^q` lies in `I^{q+n}` exactly when `a` lies in
`Iⁿ`: the class of `x^q` generates `I^q/I^{q+n}` *freely* over `A/Iⁿ`. -/
theorem smul_powQuotGen_eq_zero_iff (hx : x ∈ nonZeroDivisors A) (a : A) :
    a • powQuotGen x n q = 0 ↔ a ∈ ((Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ n : Ideal A) := by
  rw [smul_powQuotGen x n q a (mul_pow_mem_span_pow x q a), Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
  simp only [powSub, Submodule.mem_comap, Submodule.coe_subtype, Ideal.span_singleton_pow,
    Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨b, hb⟩
    refine ⟨b, ?_⟩
    have hxq : x ^ q ∈ nonZeroDivisors A := pow_mem hx q
    have h0 : (a - x ^ n * b) * x ^ q = 0 := by
      have h1 : a * x ^ q = x ^ n * b * x ^ q := by rw [hb, pow_add]; ring
      rw [sub_mul, h1, sub_self]
    exact sub_eq_zero.1 ((mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff.1 hxq).2 _ h0)
  · rintro ⟨b, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨b, by rw [pow_add]; ring⟩

/-- For `I = (x)` with `x` a nonzerodivisor, `t ↦ t·x^q` identifies `A/Iⁿ` with `I^q/I^{q+n}`.
This is the invertibility of `𝒪_X(q)`, in the one case in which the Situation of Tag 0GA6 has
`p` an isomorphism and every twist invertible. -/
noncomputable def powQuotGenEquiv (hx : x ∈ nonZeroDivisors A) :
    (A ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ n) ≃ₗ[A] powQuot (Ideal.span {x}) q n :=
  LinearEquiv.ofBijective
    (powQuotScalar (Ideal.span {x}) n q (powQuotGen x n q))
    ⟨by
      rw [injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
      intro t ht
      obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective t
      rw [powQuotScalar_apply_mk] at ht
      exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2
        ((smul_powQuotGen_eq_zero_iff x n q hx a).1 ht),
     by
      intro y
      obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := exists_smul_powQuotGen x n q y
      exact ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk _ a, powQuotScalar_apply_mk _ _ _ _ a⟩⟩

/-- The isomorphism `powQuotGenEquiv` sends the class of `t` to `t` times the class of `x^q`. -/
@[simp] theorem powQuotGenEquiv_apply (hx : x ∈ nonZeroDivisors A)
    (t : A ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ n) :
    powQuotGenEquiv x n q hx t = powQuotScalar (Ideal.span {x}) n q (powQuotGen x n q) t := rfl

end PrincipalWitness

section OfResDual

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (n : ℕ)

/-- An `A`-linear functional on the underlying `A`-module of an `A/Iⁿ`-module `M` is an element
of the dual `M^∨ = Hom_{A/Iⁿ}(M, A/Iⁿ)`: the two notions of linearity agree because
`A → A/Iⁿ` is surjective. This is `ofResHom` with `A/Iⁿ` in place of `I^q/I^{q+n}` as the
target. -/
noncomputable def ofResDual {M : ModuleCat.{u} (A ⧸ I ^ n)}
    (ψ : resModule I n M →ₗ[A] (A ⧸ I ^ n)) : Module.Dual (A ⧸ I ^ n) M where
  toFun := ψ
  map_add' := ψ.map_add
  map_smul' r z := by
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective r
    have h : ψ ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ n) a) • z) = a • ψ z := by
      rw [← ModuleCat.restrictScalars.smul_def (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ n)) (M := M) a z]
      exact ψ.map_smul a z
    rw [h, RingHom.id_apply, Algebra.smul_def]
    rfl

/-- `ofResDual` read as an element of `M^∨` viewed over `A`, which is the type the canonical
map `dualHomTensorLift` takes in its second slot; the two types are the same, and `asDual`
reads an element of the second as one of the first. -/
noncomputable def resOfResDual {M : ModuleCat.{u} (A ⧸ I ^ n)}
    (ψ : resModule I n M →ₗ[A] (A ⧸ I ^ n)) :
    resModule I n (ModuleCat.of (A ⧸ I ^ n) (Module.Dual (A ⧸ I ^ n) M)) :=
  ofResDual I n ψ

end OfResDual

section PrincipalDualHom

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (x : A) (n q : ℕ)

/-- Every element of `(I^q/I^{q+n}) ⊗_A M^∨` is `g ⊗ λ` for the generator `g` of
`powQuotGen`, when `I = (x)`: the first factor is cyclic, so the scalars can be moved onto the
second and the sums collapse. -/
theorem exists_tmul_powQuotGen
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} (A ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ n))
    (t : powTensor (Ideal.span {x}) n q
      (ModuleCat.of (A ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ n)
        (Module.Dual (A ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ n) M))) :
    ∃ lam, t = powQuotGen x n q ⊗ₜ[A] lam := by
  induction t using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul y lam =>
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := exists_smul_powQuotGen x n q y
    exact ⟨a • lam, TensorProduct.smul_tmul _ _ _⟩
  | add t₁ t₂ h₁ h₂ =>
    obtain ⟨l₁, rfl⟩ := h₁
    obtain ⟨l₂, rfl⟩ := h₂
    exact ⟨l₁ + l₂, (TensorProduct.tmul_add _ _ _).symm⟩

/-- For `I = (x)` with `x` a nonzerodivisor the canonical map
`(I^q/I^{q+n}) ⊗_A M^∨ → Hom_A(M, I^q/I^{q+n})` of Remark 0GAB is bijective.

Both sides are identified with `M^∨` by the invertibility of `𝒪_X(q)`
(`powQuotGenEquiv`), and the map becomes the identity. This is what makes
`principalCanDualSituation` a non-degenerate witness: the dictionary between homomorphisms and
sections of the dual is an isomorphism there, not a map between zero modules. -/
theorem bijective_dualHomTensorLift_span_singleton (hx : x ∈ nonZeroDivisors A)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} (A ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ n)) :
    Function.Bijective (dualHomTensorLift (Ideal.span {x}) n q M) := by
  constructor
  · rw [injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
    intro t ht
    obtain ⟨lam, rfl⟩ := exists_tmul_powQuotGen x n q M t
    rw [dualHomTensorLift_tmul] at ht
    have hlam : lam = 0 := by
      refine LinearMap.ext fun z => ?_
      have h := LinearMap.congr_fun ht z
      have h0 : (powQuotGenEquiv x n q hx) (asDual (Ideal.span {x}) n lam z) =
          (powQuotGenEquiv x n q hx) 0 := by
        rw [map_zero]; exact h
      exact (powQuotGenEquiv x n q hx).injective h0
    rw [hlam, TensorProduct.tmul_zero]
  · intro φ
    refine ⟨powQuotGen x n q ⊗ₜ[A] resOfResDual (Ideal.span {x}) n
      (((powQuotGenEquiv x n q hx).symm.toLinearMap).comp φ), ?_⟩
    rw [dualHomTensorLift_tmul]
    refine LinearMap.ext fun z => ?_
    rw [dualHom_apply]
    exact (powQuotGenEquiv x n q hx).apply_symm_apply (φ z)

/-- The dictionary of Remark 0GAB as an isomorphism, for `I = (x)` with `x` a
nonzerodivisor. -/
noncomputable def dualHomTensorEquiv (hx : x ∈ nonZeroDivisors A)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} (A ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ n)) :
    powTensor (Ideal.span {x}) n q
        (ModuleCat.of (A ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ n)
          (Module.Dual (A ⧸ (Ideal.span {x} : Ideal A) ^ n) M)) ≃ₗ[A]
      (resModule (Ideal.span {x}) n M →ₗ[A] powQuot (Ideal.span {x}) q n) :=
  LinearEquiv.ofBijective _ (bijective_dualHomTensorLift_span_singleton x n q hx M)

end PrincipalDualHom

section PrincipalCanDualSituation

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (x : A) (n c : ℕ)

/-- The `CanDualSituation` in which `I = (x)` is generated by a single nonzerodivisor. There
the blowing up `p` is an isomorphism — the case the docstring of `affineSituation` names — and
in addition every twist `𝒪_X(q)` is invertible, so that the dictionary between homomorphisms
`M → I^q/I^{q+n}` and sections of `(p^*M)^∨(q)` is the isomorphism `dualHomTensorEquiv`, `can`
is the identity, and its kernel and cokernel vanish, so that their cohomology is zero.

This witnesses that the hypotheses of `CanDualSituation` are consistent, and non-degenerately
so: `secDual` is bijective (`bijective_principalCanDualSituation_secDual`) rather than a map
between zero modules, and the modules `Hdual M q` are nonzero whenever `M^∨` is
(`nontrivial_principalCanDualSituation_Hdual`). -/
noncomputable def principalCanDualSituation (hx : x ∈ nonZeroDivisors A) (hcn : c ≤ n) :
    CanDualSituation A (Ideal.span {x}) n c :=
  { affineDualSituation (Ideal.span {x}) n c hcn with
    Hdual := fun M q => (affineDualSituation (Ideal.span {x}) n c hcn).H M.dual 0 (q : ℤ)
    Hdualtr := fun M q q' h =>
      (affineDualSituation (Ideal.span {x}) n c hcn).Htr M.dual 0 (q : ℤ) (q' : ℤ)
        (by exact_mod_cast h)
    Himg := fun M q => (affineDualSituation (Ideal.span {x}) n c hcn).H M.dual 0 (q : ℤ)
    Himgtr := fun M q q' h =>
      (affineDualSituation (Ideal.span {x}) n c hcn).Htr M.dual 0 (q : ℤ) (q' : ℤ)
        (by exact_mod_cast h)
    secDual := fun M q => (dualHomTensorEquiv x n q hx M.1).symm.toLinearMap
    evDual := fun M q hq => (affineDualSituation (Ideal.span {x}) n c hcn).ev M q hq
    evDual_secDual := fun M q _ φ => (dualHomTensorEquiv x n q hx M.1).apply_symm_apply φ
    evDual_Hdualtr := fun M q q' hq hq' h σ =>
      (affineDualSituation (Ideal.span {x}) n c hcn).ev_Htr M q q' hq hq' h
        (by exact_mod_cast h) σ
    canToImg := fun _ _ => LinearMap.id
    imgToDual := fun _ _ => LinearMap.id
    imgToDual_Himgtr := fun _ _ _ _ _ => rfl
    evDual_can := fun _ _ _ _ => rfl
    Hcoker := fun _ _ => ModuleCat.of A PUnit
    Hcokertr := fun _ _ _ _ => 0
    Hker := fun _ _ => ModuleCat.of A PUnit
    Hkertr := fun _ _ _ _ => 0
    dualToCoker := fun _ _ => 0
    canToImgδ := fun _ _ => 0
    dualToCoker_Hdualtr := fun _ _ _ _ _ => rfl
    canToImgδ_Himgtr := fun _ _ _ _ _ => rfl
    exact_imgToDual := fun _ _ σ => ⟨fun _ => ⟨σ, rfl⟩, fun _ => rfl⟩
    exact_canToImg := fun _ _ t => ⟨fun _ => ⟨t, rfl⟩, fun _ => rfl⟩
    Hcokertr_eq_zero := fun _ _ _ _ _ => rfl
    Hkertr_eq_zero := fun _ _ _ _ _ => rfl
    vanishing_Hker := fun _ _ _ => inferInstanceAs (Subsingleton PUnit) }

/-- The dictionary of the witness is bijective: in `principalCanDualSituation` the passage from
a homomorphism `φ : M → I^q/I^{q+n}` to the section `σ` of `(p^*M)^∨(q)` is an isomorphism, so
the duality step of Tag 0GAC is not a statement about zero modules there. -/
theorem bijective_principalCanDualSituation_secDual (hx : x ∈ nonZeroDivisors A) (hcn : c ≤ n)
    (M : ANCModule (Ideal.span {x}) n c) (q : ℕ) :
    Function.Bijective ((principalCanDualSituation x n c hx hcn).secDual M q) :=
  (dualHomTensorEquiv x n q hx M.1).symm.bijective

/-- The witness is not degenerate: the sections of `(p^*M)^∨` it supplies are nonzero whenever
the dual `M^∨` is. -/
theorem nontrivial_principalCanDualSituation_Hdual (hx : x ∈ nonZeroDivisors A) (hcn : c ≤ n)
    (M : ANCModule (Ideal.span {x}) n c)
    (h : Nontrivial (resModule (Ideal.span {x}) n (M.dual).1)) :
    Nontrivial ((principalCanDualSituation x n c hx hcn).Hdual M 0) :=
  nontrivial_affineH_zero (Ideal.span {x}) n (M.dual).1 h

end PrincipalCanDualSituation

